  The first draft of this line read `nothing in the library is anywhere near
  either'.  THE TABLE ABOVE CONTRADICTS IT three rows down: the RAND hosts sit
  at #{k3<=2} = 0.0%%, which MEETS the <= 50%% half of the spec outright.  The
  narration was the r45-error-3 species -- a sentence contradicting the number
  below it -- and it is corrected by RUNNING the count, not by deleting it:
    hosts meeting  #{k3<=2} <= (n-2)/2 :  33 of 66
    hosts meeting  #{k3=4}  >= 2       :  0 of 66
  SO THE BINDING HALF IS  #{k3 = 4} >= 2,  AND IT IS MET BY NOTHING.  k3 = 4 is
  draft 46.2's never-attained cell; under (COVER) an open CASE A instance is
  OBLIGED to attain it at >= 2 vertices, i.e. to carry cycles of ALL FOUR
  lengths 5, 6, 7, 8 through one step-3 frame, twice over.  Per-vertex k3 is
  read as the MAXIMUM over that vertex's frames, which is the reading most
  FAVOURABLE to the spec, so the zero above is not an artefact of the choice.

